hadiths[71]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1548","Narrated Abu Hurairah:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever among you swears"""
"1549","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:That Sa'd bin 'Ubadah asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about a vow that was due from his mother"
"1550","Salamah ibn Shabīb narrated to us, Abū al-Mughīrah narrated to us, from ʿUfayr ibn Maʿdān, from Sulaym ibn ʿĀmir, from Abū Umāmah (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The best sacrificial animal is the ram"
"1551","Narrated Abu Al-Bakhtari:\An Army from the armies of the Muslims"""
"1552","Narrated Ibn 'Asim Al-Muzani:From his father and he was a Companion who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) dispatched any army or battalion"""
"1553","Narrated Anas:\When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) set out for Khaibar"""
"1554","Narrated Abu Talhah:\When the Prophet (ﷺ) overtook a people he would stay at the outskirts of their city for three nights"""
"1555","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) burnt the palm trees of Bani Nadir and cut them down at Al-Buwairah. So Allah revealed: Whatever you cut down of their palm trees"""
"1556","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The best companions are four"""
"1557","Narrated Yazid bin Hurmuz: That Najdah Al-Haruri wrote to Ibn 'Abbas asking if the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would fight along with women"
"1558","Narrated Abu Hurairah:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever among you swears"""
"1559","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:That Sa'd bin 'Ubadah asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about a vow that was due from his mother"
"1560","Narrated by Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, from Malik ibn Anas, from Talhah ibn Abd al-Malik al-Ayli, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), who said:\n\n\Whoever vows to obey Allah"
"1561","Narrated Abu Musa: \I arrived upon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) at Khaibar along with a group of the Ash'ari tribe. He gave us shared along with those that conquered it.\"" This Hadith is Hasan Sahih Gharib. This is acted upon according to some of the people of knowledge. Al-Awza'i said: \""Whoever meets up with the Muslims before the horses"""
"1562","Narrated Abu Sa’id Al Khudri : \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited selling the spoils of war until it has been distributed.\"" There is something on this topic from Abu Hurairah. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Gharib"""
"1563","Narrated Umm Habibah bint 'Irbad bin Sariyah: From her father who told her that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited intercourse with female prisoners"
"1564","Narrated Abu Ayyub: That he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Whoever separates between a mother and her child"""
"1565","Narrated 'Ali: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said that Jibra'il had indeed descended upon him to say to him: \Tell them - meaning your Companions - to choose regarding the captives of Badr"""
"1566","Narrated 'Imran bin Husain: That the Prophet (ﷺ) ransomed two men for the Muslims with a man from the idolaters. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. The paternal uncle of Abu Al-Muhallab's name is 'Abdur Rahman bin 'Amr"
"1567","Narrated Ibn 'Umar: That a woman was found killed in one of the expeditions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"1568","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas: \I was informed by As-Sa'b bin Jaththamah who said: \"" I said: \""O Messenger of Allah our horses trampled over women and children of the idolaters.\"" He said: \""They are from their fathers.'\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"""
"1569","Narrated Abu Hurairah: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent us with an army and said: 'If you see so-and-so"""
"1570","Narrated Thawban: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever dies and he is free of three: Kibr (Pride)"""
"1571","Narrated Thawban:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever's soul departs from his body while he is free of three: Kanz (buried treasure)"""
"1572","Narrated Simak Abu Rumail Al-Hanafi: \I heard Ibn 'Abbas saying: 'Umar bin Al-Khattab narrated to me that he said: \""It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah! So-and-so has been martyred.' He said: \""No! I saw him in the fire of garment he pilfered from the spoils of war.' He said: 'Stand up O 'Umar! Call out that no one enters paradise except the believers.' Three times.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih Gharib"""
"1573","Narrated Anas: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to go to battle with Umm Sulaim"""
"1574","Qutaybah narrated to us, that ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not make vows (nadhr)"
"1575","Narrated Anas: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to go to battle with Umm Sulaim, and other women with her, from the Ansar, who would give water and attend to the wounded."" [Abu 'Eisa said:] There is something on this topic from Ar-Rabi' bin Mu'awwidh. This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"
"1576","Narrated Abu Bakrah: \The Prophet (ﷺ) was met by some affair that made him happy"""
"1577","Narrated Abu Al-Faid: \I heard Sulaim bin 'Amir saying: 'There was a treaty between Mu'awiyah and the people of Rome. He was making an expedition into their lands so that when the period of the treaty was expires he would attack them. So when a man upon an animal' - or - 'upon a horse said: \""Allahu Akbar! Fulfillment not betrayal!\"" - and it turned out to be 'Amr bin 'Abasah - Mu'awiyah asked him about that. He said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Whoever has a treaty between himself and a people"""
"1578","Narrated Ibn 'Umar: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed the one who betrays will have a banner erected for him on the Day of Judgement.\"" [He said:] There are narrations on this topic from 'Ali"""
"1579","# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Narrated by Thābit ibn al-Ḍaḥḥāk (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:**\n\nThe Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n> **\Whoever swears an oath by a religion other than Islām"
"1580","Narrated Samurah bin Jundab: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Kill the elder men among the idolaters and spare the Sharkh amont them.\"" And the Sharkh are the boys who did not begin to grow pubic hair. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. Hajjaj bin Artah narrated similarly from Qatadah"""
"1581","Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: al-Awza'i narrated to us: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever among you swears an oath and says in his oath"
"1582","Qutaybah narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd ibn 'Utbah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about a vow that his mother had made but had passed away before fulfilling it. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Fulfill it on her behalf.\"" Abu 'Isa said: This is a hasan sahih hadith."""
"1583","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us: 'Imran ibn 'Uyaynah—he is the brother of Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah—narrated to us, from Husayn, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abu Umamah and other Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \Any Muslim man who frees a Muslim male slave shall be his ransom from the Fire; every limb of the freed slave shall be a ransom for a corresponding limb of the master. And any Muslim man who frees two Muslim female slaves shall be his ransom from the Fire; every limb of the two shall be a ransom for a corresponding limb of the master. And any Muslim woman who frees a Muslim female slave shall be her ransom from the Fire; every limb of the freed slave shall be a ransom for a corresponding limb of the mistress.\"" Abu 'Isa said: This is a hasan sahih gharib hadith from this chain. Abu 'Isa further commented: The hadith indicates that freeing male slaves is more meritorious than freeing female slaves"
"1584","Narrated Simak Abu Rumail Al-Hanafi: \I heard Ibn 'Abbas saying: 'Umar bin Al-Khattab narrated to me that he said: \""It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah! So-and-so has been martyred.' He said: \""No! I saw him in the fire of garment he pilfered from the spoils of war.' He said: 'Stand up O 'Umar! Call out that no one enters paradise except the believers.' Three times.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih Gharib"""
"1585","Narrated Anas: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to go to battle with Umm Sulaim"""
"1586","Narrated by al-Ansari, narrated by Ma'n, narrated to me Malik ibn Anas, from Humayd, from Anas, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) set out for Khaybar, he arrived at night. Whenever he came to a people at night, he would not attack them until morning. When morning came, the Jews came out with their spades and baskets. When they saw him, they said, \Muhammad and his army have come! By Allah"
"1587","Narrated 'Iyad bin Himar: That he gave the Prophet (ﷺ) a gift or a camel"
"1588","Narrated Abu Bakrah: \The Prophet (ﷺ) was met by some affair that made him happy"""
"1589","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\\n\\nThat the Prophet (ﷺ) said: Indeed a woman grants (assurances of protection) to a people - meaning it is to be honored - from the Muslims. \\n"
"1590","Narrated Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet ﷺ said:\n\n\I have been favoured over the prophets with six things: I have been given the jawāmiʿ al-kalim (the concise"
"1591","and Al-Walid bin Rabah heard from Abu Hurairah, and he is Muqarib (average) in Hadith. \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 1579 Arabic Hadees: 1579\""1592"""
"1592","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Sulaym ibn Akhdar, similarly. And in this chapter there are narrations from Mujammi' ibn Jariyah, Ibn 'Abbas, and Ibn Abi 'Amrah from his father. And this hadith of Ibn 'Umar is hasan sahih. And the practice is upon this among the majority of the people of knowledge from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ and others. And it is the view of Sufyan al-Thawri, al-Awza'i, Malik ibn Anas, Ibn al-Mubarak, al-Shafi'i, Ahmad, and Ishaq. They said: For the horseman there are three shares: one share for him and two shares for his horse. And for the foot soldier there is one share."
"1593","Narrated Ibn 'Umar: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed the one who betrays will have a banner erected for him on the Day of Judgement.\"" [He said:] There are narrations on this topic from 'Ali"""
"1594","# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Qutaybah narrated to us; Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from Yazīd ibn Hurmuz, that Najdah al-Ḥarūrī wrote to Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما asking him: \Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ take women along on military expeditions"
"1595","Narrated Samurah bin Jundab: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Kill the elder men among the idolaters and spare the Sharkh amont them.\"" And the Sharkh are the boys who did not begin to grow pubic hair. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. Hajjaj bin Artah narrated similarly from Qatadah"""
"1596","Narrated 'Atiyyah Al-Qurazi: \We were presented to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on the day of (the battle of) Quraizah. Whoever had pubic hair was killed and whoever did not was left to his way. I was of those who did not have pubic hair so I was left to my way.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. This is acted upon according to some of the people of knowledge. They consider pubic hair an indication of the age of responsibility"""
"1597","It is narrated from al-Zuhri that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, allotted a share of the spoils of war to a group of Jews who fought alongside him. Qutaybah ibn Sa'id related this to us; 'Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id informed us from 'Azrah ibn Thabit from al-Zuhri with this chain. This is a hasan gharib hadith."
"1598","Narrated Bajalah bin 'Abdah : \I was a scribe for Jaz' bin Mu'awiyah at Manadhir when 'Umar's letter came to us (saying): 'Inspect the Zoroastrians around you to take the Jizyah from them. For indeed 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Awf informed me that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took the Jizyah from the Zoroastrians of Hajar.'\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan"""
"1599","Narrated Bajalah: That 'Umar would not take the Jizyah from the Zoroastrians until 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Awf informed him that the Prophet (ﷺ) took Jizyah from the Zoroastrians of Hajar.\ There is more dialogue in the Hadith than this. And this Hadith is Hasan Sahih"""
"1600","It was narrated to us that Hannad said: It was narrated to us by Ibn Al-Mubarak, from Haywah ibn Shurayh, who said: I heard Rabi'ah ibn Yazid Al-Dimashqi saying: Abu Idris Al-Khulani, 'A'idhullah ibn 'Ubaydullah, informed me that he heard Abu Tha'labah Al-Khushni saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said, \O Messenger of Allah"
"1601","Narrated 'Uqbah bin 'Amir: \I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! We come across a people and they do not host us"""
"1602","# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Hannād narrated to us** — Ibn Abī az-Zinād narrated to us, from his father, from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah, from Ibn ʿAbbāṣ (may Allāh be pleased with them both), that the Prophet ﷺ took as his personal spoil (*tanaffala*) his sword Dhū al-Faqār on the day of Badr, and it was the same sword regarding which he saw a vision on the day of Uḥud.\n\nThis is a *ḥasan gharīb* hadith. We only know it through this chain of narration, from the hadith of Ibn Abī az-Zinād.\n\nThe scholars have differed regarding the granting of a bonus share (*nafl*) from the one-fifth (*khums*). Mālik ibn Anas said: \It has not reached me that the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ granted a bonus share in all of his military expeditions; however"
"1603","# Hadith Translation\n\n**Narrated Abu Qatada (may Allah be pleased with him):**\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n**\Whoever kills an enemy combatant for whom there is clear proof (of being a lawful target in battle)"
"1604","Narrated Yazid bin Abi 'Ubaid: \I said to Salamah bin Al-Akwa': \""For what did you pledge to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on the Day of Al-Hudaibiyyah?\"" He said: \""For death.\"" This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"""
"1605","Narrated Ibn 'Umar: \We used to pledge to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to hear and obey.\"" So he would say to us: \""As much as you are able.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"""
"1606","Narrated Jabir bin ‘Abdullah : \We did not pledge to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for death"""
"1607","Narrated Abu Hurairah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Three will not be spoken to by Allah on the Day of Judgement"""
"1608","Narrated Jabir: \A slave came to give the pledge to the Prophet (ﷺ) for Hijrah"""
"1609","Ibn Al-Munkadir heard Umaimah bin Ruqaiqah saying:\I pledged to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) along with some women. He said to us: 'In as much as you are able and capable.' I said: 'Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us than we are to ourselves"""
"1610","Narrated Al-Bara' : \We used to say that the participants of Badr on the Day of Badr were like the number of companions of Talut"""
"1611","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\\n\\nThat the Prophet (ﷺ) said to a delegation from 'Abdul-Qais: I order you to give the Khumus from your spoils of war. \\n\\nHe said: There is a story with this Hadith\\n\\n[Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 1599 Arabic Hadees: 1599\""1612"""
"1612","Ibn Abi 'Umar narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Ayyub narrated to us from Abu Qilabah, from his uncle, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet ﷺ ransomed two Muslim men for one polytheist man. Abu 'Isa said: This is a hasan sahih hadith. And the uncle of Abu Qilabah is Abu al-Muhallab, his name is 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr, and it is said Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr. And Abu Qilabah's name is 'Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Jarmi. And the practice is upon this among the majority of the people of knowledge from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ and others: that the Imam may grant amnesty to whomever he wishes of the captives, kill whomever he wishes of them, and ransom whomever he wishes. And some people of knowledge preferred killing over ransom. And al-Awza'i said: It reached me that this verse is abrogated: His saying, Exalted is He: ""Then either grace afterwards or ransom"" (47:4) was abrogated by: ""And kill them wherever you find them"" (2:191). Hammad narrated that to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from al-Awza'i. Ishaq ibn Mansur said: I said to Ahmad: ""When a captive is taken, is it more beloved to you that he be killed or ransomed?"" He said: ""If they are able to ransom him, there is no harm in it. And if he is killed, I know no harm in it."" Ishaq ibn Ibrahim said: ""Killing (ithkhan) is more beloved to me, unless he is well-known (for status), then I hope through him to ransom many."""
"1613","Narrated Anas: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever plunders then he is not of us.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih Gharib as a Hadith of Anas"""
"1614","Narrated Abu Hurairah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not precede the Jews and the Christians with the Salam. And if one you meets one of them in the path"""
"1615","Narrated Ibn 'Umar: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed when a Jew gives Salam to one of you"""
"1616","Narrated Qais bin Abu Hazim: From Jarir bin 'Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent a military expedition to Khath'am. So some people (living there) sought safety by prostrating"
"1617","Narrated Qais bin Abu Hazim: Similar to the narration of Abu Mu'aqiyah (no. 1604) but he did not mention in it: \from Jarir\"" in it"""
"1618","Narrated 'Umar bin Al-Khattab:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \If I live - if Allah wills - I will expel the Jews and the Christians from the Arabian Peninsula"""
